span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l11 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There is a proposed syntax =
simplification on the openembedded-architecture list with a patch on =
bitbake-devel. This would phase out the use of append/prepend/remove =
operators with +=3D/=3D+ and mean it would just work with =
&#8220;=3D&#8221; alone. We&#8217;ve not recommended this combination =
and it removes a redundancy which confuses new =
users.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l11 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There will be some =
infrastructure down time at the end of the year for the autobuilder and =
NAS, likely between the 26th and 31st December. This will affect the =
autobuilder workers, downloads and sstate shares from the project but =
not websites or git services. Last time we had a NAS outage it caused =
some issues so we are trying to ensure those issues are fixed in the =
stable branches and master with mirroring in place for key things like =
uninative before then. If anyone is aware of any other failure modes we =
need to address, please let us know.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l11 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Workarounds for the github =
protocol changes have been merged to all stable branches and to master =
with url changes also being made in many =
cases.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l11 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We have seen a drop in the =
number of patches in &#8220;Pending&#8221; state again this week. Many =
thanks to everyone who has taken the time to review patch status and =
handle accordingly.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l11 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>5.15 kernel headers and kernels =
have been merged.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l11 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There have been a number of =
small but potentially useful bitbake fixes to file checksum tracking, =
runall option handling and hung parsing =
threads.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l11 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent issues continue to =
rise and help is very much welcome on these issues. You can see the list =
of failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the =
&#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
